  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian national football team is currently conducting a training camp in Bali under the direction of head coach John Herdman. The camp serves as a primary evaluation period for emerging domestic talents, such as Arlyansyah Abdulmanan and Zanadin Fariz, who have been identified as key prospects for the 2027 SEA Games. As the coaching staff refines the squad, focus has shifted toward building a competitive roster, which includes monitoring both local players and potential naturalized candidates. Separately, the women's national team, led by Alen Stajcic, has also announced a 25-player squad for upcoming friendly matches against Bhutan, highlighting an active period for national football development. The ongoing training activities are part of a broader strategy to solidify the team's composition as officials continue to evaluate diverse professional backgrounds and eligibility for future international competitions.",
